// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`triage handoff template snapshots > 'duo' 'planner' → 'triage' renders the complete contract 1`] = `
"> ⚠️ **Template notice — not part of the message. Do not copy this notice into your handoff.**
> Recipient visibility: the \`triage\` agent receives only the text inside your \`handoff --next-role="triage"\` command. It cannot see anything you write in this agent session, or tool output. Put your complete deliverable in the handoff message.

Handoff template \`planner\` → \`triage\` (copy only the body sections below; do not copy this line, the notice, or the instructions after the body):

The automatically injected \`<user-message>\` is the authoritative request. Pass the reported bug, observed and expected behavior, reproduction details and commands, relevant constraints, and the files or symbols already suspected. Ask triage to investigate and report only. Triage may inspect code and attempt a focused automated regression test as evidence, but must not edit implementation files or implement a fix.

Use this for every reported bug (something broken or behaving differently than expected) before any fix is implemented.

After completing the investigation, triage must return the evidence-backed report to \`planner\` with the normal handoff command.

\`\`\`bash
chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="<chatroom-id>" --role="planner" --next-role="triage" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`"
`;

exports[`triage handoff template snapshots > 'duo' 'triage' → 'planner' renders the complete contract 1`] = `
"> ⚠️ **Template notice — not part of the message. Do not copy this notice into your handoff.**
> Recipient visibility: the \`planner\` agent receives only the text inside your \`handoff --next-role="planner"\` command. It cannot see anything you write in this agent session, or tool output. Put your complete deliverable in the handoff message.

Handoff template \`triage\` → \`planner\` (copy only the body sections below; do not copy this line, the notice, or the instructions after the body):

Instructions (not part of the message): Return a complete, evidence-backed investigation of the authoritative reported bug. Triage is advisory: do not edit implementation files or implement the proposed fix. Begin with the \`## Summary\` section, then use the remaining sections below in order. Use \`###\` for sub-items within a section. Cite concrete repository paths and symbols, observed behavior, commands, and test output. Distinguish confirmed findings from hypotheses; never claim a test proved behavior unless its failing assertion demonstrates the report. Redact every secret in quoted output as \`<REDACTED>\`, and quote only the lines that carry the signal.

## Summary
<briefly state the diagnosis and whether the root cause was confirmed or remains a hypothesis>

## Reported behavior
<state the reported symptoms and expected behavior, including reproduction details and constraints recovered from the request or relevant history>

## Root cause
<first list 3 to 5 ranked hypotheses, each as "If <X> is the cause, then <changing Y> removes the symptom (or <changing Z> makes it worse)", before testing any of them; then state the confirmed or hypothesized cause, tracing ownership, data, and control flow with concrete repository paths and symbols; for each hypothesis, say whether it was tested and the outcome; check memory/ decision-log entries and docs/ for whether the behavior is documented as intended before calling it a defect; label the finding confirmed or hypothesis>

## Reproduction attempt
<give the one command that drives the user's exact symptom, its observed output (redacted), and how many times it ran; state whether it is deterministic, or the reproduction rate for flaky behavior; give the minimal scenario, listing each input, caller, or configuration removed and whether the symptom stayed; for slow or regressed performance, the baseline measurement taken before any change; if no reproducing command could be built, say so, list what was tried, and name exactly what is needed to proceed (environment access, a redacted captured artifact, or permission to add temporary instrumentation); never fabricate proof>

## Proposed immediate fix
<recommend the smallest appropriate change, naming the likely files and the specific change; do not implement it; then name the regression-test seam: the public interface where a failing regression test belongs, with one line on what it catches and what it misses; if only a shallow seam exists (the bug needs several callers or a longer chain of calls to trigger), say so and add it under Systemic issues>

## Systemic issues
<list each separate systemic concern with repository evidence, impact, and follow-up concern, or write exactly: None observed.>

## Work completed
<state the code paths inspected and every test or reproduction action taken, including results>

Instructions after the body (not part of the message): run the normal handoff command to \`planner\` with the complete body above, then stop.

\`\`\`bash
chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="<chatroom-id>" --role="triage" --next-role="planner" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`"
`;

